      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Exact Perron inversion for a generalized Dirichlet series is justified by subtracting the already counted terms and shifting the remaining tail by its first omitted exponent, which supplies horizontal-edge decay; finite vertical truncation instead yields an approximate step selector with an explicit loss concentrated near the cutoff.",
