    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_4061a79e541e982a7cc2ac43d8c210622a1e97b59d61ac30638078e6f9ff9797",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "Prime powers are native coefficients of logarithmic-derivative and explicit-formula representations, and Möbius inversion is needed only when the target is primes alone. In log-value problems their status is family-dependent: higher powers and squares are controlled errors in the height family under RH, while squares produce the leading recentering term in the quadratic-character family under GRH.",
