      "proposed_content": "A bounded zero computation can certify every zero in its rectangle while saying nothing by itself about global RH or a limiting Gram-block law. Separately, iterated-logarithm growth explains how an unbounded zero-driven oscillation can remain hidden behind a finite-range bias throughout feasible computation.",
